{
  "slug": "cauchy-schwarz-oq-02-oq-04",
  "title": "Operator-Norm and Positive-Operator Cauchy–Schwarz",
  "phase": "COMPLETED",
  "status": "completed",
  "tier": "B",
  "path": "full",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "For a bounded operator T on an inner-product space over an RCLike field, ‖⟪T x, y⟫‖ ≤ ‖T‖·‖x‖·‖y‖; and for a positive symmetric T, ⟪T x, y⟫² ≤ ⟪T x, x⟫·⟪T y, y⟫.",
    "plain": "Sharpen Cauchy–Schwarz when one vector is the image of a bounded operator T: the inner product is controlled by the operator norm. Develop the numerical-radius bound, submultiplicativity, the adjoint form, recovery of classical Cauchy–Schwarz, and the positive-operator (Kadison–Schwarz) inequality.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Connects the elementary Cauchy–Schwarz inequality to operator theory (numerical radius, Kadison–Schwarz) over a general RCLike field (ℝ or ℂ).",
      "Shows operator-norm Cauchy–Schwarz is one substitution away from the scalar case, and that a positive symmetric operator induces its own semi-inner-product Cauchy–Schwarz."
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "Operator-norm Cauchy–Schwarz ‖⟪T x, y⟫‖ ≤ ‖T‖·‖x‖·‖y‖ over any RCLike field.",
      "Numerical-radius bound ‖⟪T x, x⟫‖ ≤ ‖T‖·‖x‖² (w(T) ≤ ‖T‖); submultiplicativity under composition and scaling; adjoint form.",
      "Recovery of classical scalar Cauchy–Schwarz from the identity operator (‖id‖ ≤ 1).",
      "Positive-operator (Kadison–Schwarz) inequality ⟪T x, y⟫² ≤ ⟪T x, x⟫·⟪T y, y⟫ for positive symmetric T, plus its square-root form, via a discriminant argument."
    ],
    "open": [],
    "goal": "Formalize the operator-norm and positive-operator strengthenings of Cauchy–Schwarz and recover the classical inequality as a special case."
  },
